    "description": "Given the placement scenario at Goldman Sachs, solve the following Predecessor/Successor problem:\n\nYou are given an input sequence representing transactional or relational data. Implement an optimal algorithmic function to evaluate the predecessor/successor criteria, handling all boundary edge cases.\n\nExample 1:\nInput: data = [2, 7, 11, 15], target = 9\nOutput: [0, 1]\nExplanation: Indices 0 and 1 sum to 9.\n\nConstraints:\n- 1 <= N <= 2 * 10^5\n- Time Limit: 1.0 second\n- Memory Limit: 256 MB",
    "topic": "Binary Search Trees",
    "subtopic": "Predecessor/Successor",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
